[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Persistence Eradication
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l [?2004h> #### Step 2.1: Eradicate Cron Persistence
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Remove automated re-dropper cron entry.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Backup current crontab and remove malicious root crontab entry.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   cp /var/spool/cron/root /root/quarantine_/cron_root.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i '/198.51.100.78/d' /var/spool/cron/root
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `crontab -l -u root`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-05`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 2.2: Eradicate Systemd Service Persistence
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Disable persistent malicious systemd service.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Stop, disable, quarantine, and reload systemd daemon.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl stop system-update-helper.service || true
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl disable system-update-helper.service || true
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service /root/quarantine_/system-update-helper.service.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl daemon-reload
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl reset-failed
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `systemctl status system-update-helper.service` (returns inactive/not-found)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-06`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 2.3: Eradicate Shell Initialization Persistence
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Remove malicious shell hook in root account.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Backup `/root/.bashrc` and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing line.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   cp /root/.bashrc /root/quarantine_/bashrc.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i '/PROMPT_COMMAND/d' /root/.bashrc
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `grep -i PROMPT_COMMAND /root/.bashrc` (returns empty)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/root/.bashrc`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 2.4: Eradicate Privileged Backdoor (Sudoers)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Remove unauthenticated root access for `devops` user.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Quarantine `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` backdoor file.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /etc/sudoers.d/devops /root/quarantine_/devops_sudoers.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `sudo -l -U devops` (verify `NOPASSWD: ALL` is no longer granted)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: System Hardening & Recovery
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 3.1: Account Credential Rotation & Session Invalidation
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Revoke compromised credentials and terminate unauthorized sessions.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Reset passwords for `root` and `devops`, kill active sessions.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   passwd -l root
[?2004l[?2004h>   openssl rand -base64 24 | passwd --stdin devops
[?2004l[?2004h>   pkill -u devops
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `passwd -S root` and `passwd -S devops`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 3.2: SSH Server Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Prevent password brute-forcing and unauthorized root login.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Update `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to enforce secure baseline settings.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i 's/^PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl restart sshd
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `sshd -T | grep -E 'permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication'` (should show `permitrootlogin no` and `passwordauthentication no`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 3.3: MySQL Server Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective**: Restrict database exposure to local host only.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Modify `/etc/my.cnf` to bind MySQL to loopback interface.
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i '/\[mysqld\]/a bind-address = 127.0.0.1' /etc/my.cnf
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl restart mysqld
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: `ss -tulpn | grep 3306` (should listen on `127.0.0.1:3306`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Post-Remediation Verification Checklist
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify no processes running from `/tmp` or hidden directories (`ps aux | grep tmp`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify root crontab is clear of untrusted external scripts (`crontab -l`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify no custom enabled systemd services persist (`systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify `/root/.bashrc` and `/etc/bashrc` contain no `PROMPT_COMMAND` hooks (`grep -rn PROMPT_COMMAND /etc/bashrc /root/.bashrc`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify `/etc/sudoers` and `/etc/sudoers.d/` contain no unauthorized `NOPASSWD` entries (`grep -rn NOPASSWD /etc/sudoers*`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify SSH daemon blocks root logins and password auth (`sshd -T`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - [ ] Verify MySQL listens on `127.0.0.1` (`ss -tulpn`)
